**1. Additional Benchmark: BringUpBench**

Following Reviewer CTua's suggestion, we have incorporated an additional real-world benchmark, **BringUpBench**, into our evaluation. Unlike ExeBench, BringUpBench consists of **standalone libraries used for CPUs/compilers/OS testing with minimal reliance on user-defined types**. This dataset ensures that the evaluation focuses on code logic recovery rather than the impossible task of guessing unrecoverable type names. We compiled, decompiled, and executed tests on 505 functions from this suite. 

| Re-compilability rates         | O0     | O1     | O2     | O3     | Avg   |
|----------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|
| IDA              | 28.4  | 23.2  | 23.3  | 19.4  | 23.6  |
| SK2Decompile         | 44.3  | 44.5  | 42.1  | 38.3  | 42.3  |

| Re-executability rates      | O0     | O1     | O2     | O3     | Avg   |
|----------------------|--------|--------|--------|--------|--------|
| IDA              | 25.4  | 21.6  | 21.4  | 18.3  | 21.7  |
| SK2Decompile         | 34.3  | 29.1  | 24.9  | 19.7  | 27.0  |


Quantitative results on BringUpBench confirm that SK2Decompile surpasses the industry-standard decompiler, IDA. Specifically, our method achieves a re-compilability rate of 42.3%—a substantial 79.5% relative increase over IDA. Furthermore, SK2Decompile demonstrates superior functional recovery with a re-executability rate of 27.0%, outperforming IDA by 24.3%.

